{"id":224328592448208,"type":"artist","name":"Teenage Fanclub","artist":null,"year":1989,"weight":14,"info":{"tags":["power pop","indie","Scottish","indie rock","alternative"],"country":"GB","begin":"1989","kind":"Group","similar":["Velvet Crush","Big Star","The Lemonheads","Super Furry Animals","The Posies","Guided by Voices","Superchunk","Sugar","The Charlatans","Sebadoh"],"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/TeenageFanclub001.jpg?width=500","bio":"Pop en estado puro. Guitarras cruzadas y magnífico directo.\n\nBanda escocesa formada a finales de los 80, editaron su primer disco, \"A catholic education\", en 1990 para el sello Paperhouse. Aunque en un principio se dejaron llevar más por el \"shoegazing\" más ensimismado, pronto sacaron a relucir su brillante vena pop y en 1991 publicaron el excelente \"Bandwagonesque\" ya en el sello Creation. A este bombazo popero de primera magnitud le siguieron obras de manual como \"13\" (1993), \"Grand Prix\" (1995) y \"Songs from Northern Britain\" (1997)."},"works":[{"id":250773054812182,"type":"album","name":"Bandwagonesque","artist":"Teenage Fanclub","year":1991,"weight":22,"yt":"rqYibZeafg8","src":"books,charts,musthear","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Scaruffi)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":222945056519976,"name":"Sputnikmusic Best Albums 1991","rank":109,"scaruffi":null},{"id":192934750972716,"name":"1001 Albums You Must Hear Before You Die","rank":705,"scaruffi":null},{"id":22099031234954,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Power Pop","rank":34,"scaruffi":null},{"id":161051722508702,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Jangle Pop","rank":25,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":4}},{"id":276800319679507,"type":"album","name":"Grand Prix","artist":"Teenage Fanclub","year":1995,"weight":11,"yt":"2cRiDzGPt58","src":"charts,musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":238350566072075,"name":"Pitchfork: The 50 Best Britpop Albums","rank":36,"scaruffi":null},{"id":22099031234954,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Power Pop","rank":20,"scaruffi":null},{"id":161051722508702,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Jangle Pop","rank":15,"scaruffi":null},{"id":209707313206254,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Pop Rock","rank":147,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":4}},{"id":11673770222405,"type":"song","name":"Sparky's Dream","artist":"Teenage Fanclub","year":1995,"weight":2,"yt":"K4XVIKVYjGo","src":"singles","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":252802402426228,"name":"Triple J Hottest 100 · 1995","rank":60,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":235443544637125,"type":"album","name":"Songs From Northern Britain","artist":"Teenage Fanclub","year":2000,"weight":5,"yt":"-W8oMfo84Y0","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":22099031234954,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Power Pop","rank":39,"scaruffi":null},{"id":161051722508702,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Jangle Pop","rank":30,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":2}}],"members":[],"member_of":[],"genres":[],"album_genres":[{"id":121661734395550,"type":"genre","name":"Power Pop","n":4},{"id":15906669628272,"type":"genre","name":"Jangle Pop","n":4},{"id":8412226417108,"type":"genre","name":"Indie Rock","n":2},{"id":210192360016800,"type":"genre","name":"Alternative Rock","n":1},{"id":185670346256268,"type":"genre","name":"rock","n":1},{"id":30277598324326,"type":"genre","name":"pop","n":1},{"id":18872195504512,"type":"genre","name":"Pop Rock","n":1}],"labels":[],"album_labels":[],"own_scenes":[],"scenes":[{"id":193634530822272,"name":"Brit-pop y post-pop","book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","start":1990,"end":2001,"desc":"Como tantas veces, el fenómeno más publicitado es el menos interesante: un «brit-pop» de grupos terriblemente parecidos y tediosos, sin apenas imaginación. Lo anticipan Lightning Seeds, La's, Teenage Fanclub y Heavenly; estalla con Boo Radleys, Blur (Parklife) y Oasis (el «farol» que mejor personifica la moda). Suede y el glam-pop (Super Furry Animals, Placebo), las excepciones de High Llamas (Hawaii) y Supergrass, el revival mod (Ocean Colour Scene, Wildhearts), Elastica, Sleeper, las Spice Girls; Trembling Blue Stars, Tindersticks, Delgados. El post-pop de Radiohead, «la banda más publicitada y sobrevalorada de la década», cuyo OK Computer es una obra maestra del falso vanguardismo; Coldplay, Travis.","color":"#f472b6","family":"Pop, power-pop y synth-pop","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#britpop"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":250773054812182,"artist":"Teenage Fanclub","artist_id":224328592448208,"title":"Bandwagonesque","year":1991,"ess":0,"yt":"dtXrIrtTyyQ","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Brit-pop y post-pop","scene_id":193634530822272,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#britpop","chapters":["Sección 6.11"],"pages":[[1,270,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":270,"text":"…Seeds, with their retro' classic Cloudcuckooland (1990), and La's, with La's (1990), specializing in sculpting memorable and unassuming melodies. Teenage Fanclub produced one of the best imitations of Big Star with Bandwagonesque (1991). Heavenly (2) inherited the Primitives' passion for melodious simplicity.…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Similar to Oasis","body":"Teenage Fanclub was among the bands that started to appear, sounding similar to Oasis, demonstrating the latter's popularity and influence within the Britpop scene. \"The Oasis approach proved to be so popular that they started to hear and see similar bands.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of Alt Rock: Chapter 12","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DSvoppf1dGY"}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":250773054812182,"type":"album","name":"Bandwagonesque","work_year":1991,"list_id":19293475097